<?xml version="1.0"?>

<guion>
    <slide titulo="Stonefish Simulator">
        <contenido>
            <html>
                <h2>Benvingut / Bienvenidos / Welcome </h2>
                <p>
                    This is the Workshop of the
                    Stonefish simulator
                    for marine Robotics
                </p>
                <p>For ROSCON 2025 @ Barcelona-Spain</p>
                <p>Powered by ROS 2, passion for robotics, and a lots of birra</p>
            </html>
        </contenido>
        <image_topic>/bluerov_roscon/front_camera/image_color</image_topic>
        <robot_pose xyz="0.0 0.0 0.1" rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0"/>
    </slide>
    <slide titulo="Introduction.A">
        <contenido>
            <html>
                <p>Stonefish is a state of the art simulator for underwater robotics, focusing strongly in hydrodynamics, GPU accelerated graphics, and robot hardware simulation. </p>
            </html>
        </contenido>
        <image_topic>/bluerov_roscon/back_camera/image_color</image_topic>
        <robot_pose xyz="0.0 0.0 2.0" rpy="0.0 0.0 0.0"/>
    </slide>

    <slide titulo="Introduction.B">
        <contenido>
            <html>
                <p>Its a ligthweigth, standalone C++ library, which offers easy to use API to build dynamic simulations, or also can be defined through simple descriptions in a XML file</p>
            </html>
        </contenido>
        <image_topic>/bluerov_roscon/back_camera/image_color</image_topic>
    </slide>

    <slide titulo="Introduction.C">
        <contenido>
            <html>
                <p>And with seamless integration, it also pivots on the foundations of ROS (1 and 2!), allowing to develop and test many marine robotics applications that have high physics requirements.</p>
            </html>
        </contenido>
        <image_topic>/bluerov_roscon/back_camera/image_color</image_topic>
    </slide>

    <slide titulo="Vision sensors">
        <contenido>
            <html>
                <p>Stonefish offers plenty of sensors that allows the robot to understand its environment, for all type of different tasks.</p>
                <p>Camera like sensors</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Color camera</li>
                    <li>Depth camera</li>
                    <li>Event Based camera</li>
                    <li>Thermal camera</li>
                    <li>Optical flow camera</li>
                </ul>
            </html>
        </contenido>
        <image_topic>/bluerov_roscon/side_camera/image_color</image_topic>
        <robot_pose xyz="2.5 0.7 5.5" rpy="0.0 0.0 -1.5708"/>
    </slide>

    <slide titulo="Color camera">
        <contenido>
            <html>
                <p>
                    Basic RGB camera sensor, with parameters such as:
                    <ul>
                        <li>Publish rate</li>
                        <li>Resolution and FoV</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </html>
        </contenido>
        <image_topic>/bluerov_roscon/front_camera/image_color</image_topic>
        <robot_pose xyz="2.5 0.7 5.5" rpy="0.0 0.0 -1.5708"/>
    </slide>

    <slide titulo="Depth camera">
        <contenido>
            <html>
                <p>Depth camera which outputs a grayscale image where black and white represent the minimum and maximum values for depth in the image. Params: </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Publish rate</li>
                    <li>Resolution and FoV</li>
                    <li>Depth min and max values</li>
                    <li>Noise in the depth measurements</li>
                </ul>
            </html>
        </contenido>
        <image_topic>/bluerov_roscon/depth/image_depth</image_topic>
        <robot_pose xyz="2.5 0.7 5.5" rpy="0.0 0.0 -1.5708"/>
    </slide>

    <slide titulo="Event based camera">
        <contenido>
            <html>
                <p>
                    Each pixel detects variations in brightness and generates an “event”, composed of polarity, and a time stamp.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Because of its simplicity its has good performance in low ligth enviroments, and also in fast paced motions. (widely used in aerial drones for fast motions).
                </p>
            </html>
        </contenido>
        <image_topic>/bluerov_roscon/event_image</image_topic>
        <robot_pose xyz="2.5 0.7 5.5" rpy="0.0 0.0 -1.5708"/>
    </slide>

    <slide titulo="Sonar based sensors">
        <contenido>
            <html>
                <p>Sonar based sensors, widely used in the underwater realm, exploiting sound travel properties</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Multibeam sonar</li>
                    <li>Forward looking sonar (FLS)</li>
                    <li>Mechanical scanning imaging sonar (MSIS)</li>
                    <li>Side scan sonar (SSS)</li>
                </ul>
            </html>
        </contenido>
        <image_topic>/bluerov_roscon/back_camera/image_color</image_topic>
        <robot_pose xyz="2.5 6.0 4.0" rpy="0.0 0.0 -1.57"/>
    </slide>

    <slide titulo="Mechanical scanning imaging sonar">
        <contenido>
            <html>
                <p>Mechanical sonar description</p>
            </html>
        </contenido>
        <image_topic>/bluerov_roscon/msis/display</image_topic>
        <robot_pose xyz="2.5 6.0 4.0" rpy="0.0 0.0 -1.57"/>
    </slide>

    <slide titulo="Forward looking sonar">
        <contenido>
            <html>
                <p>Forward looking sonar description</p>
            </html>
        </contenido>
        <image_topic>/bluerov_roscon/fls/display</image_topic>
        <robot_pose xyz="2.5 6.0 4.0" rpy="0.0 0.0 -1.57"/>
    </slide>

    <slide titulo="Virtual sensors">
        <contenido>
            <html>
                <p>Even sensors used only for in simulation purposes</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Segmentation camera</li>
                    <li>Optical flow camera</li>
                </ul>
            </html>
        </contenido>
        <image_topic>/bluerov_roscon/label_cam/image_color</image_topic>
        <robot_pose xyz="2.5 5.0 2.0" rpy="0.0 0.0 -1.57"/>
    </slide>
</guion>